        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-18T19:08:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Does Reach increase the Origin of attacks?&nbsp;<span>For instance, does Bunker's +3 Reach increase how far his Grenades can fire? I played a game with Adam during GenCon where we did this, but it seemed odd and wanted some quick clarification. From the rules, it only mentions that Reach effects die making range.</span></p><p>Also: Vertex Attacks: For Grenade Launcher, do you count hexes for the Origin then make the attack on one of the vertices of that hex or do you count vertices away from Bunker and make the attack on the vertex you end up on?&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:13.965Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 11019,
        "topic_slug": "reach-and-origin-and-vertex-attacks",
